{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463849-being-frozen-in-time-with-accents","id":1463849,"title":"Being Frozen in Time... with Accents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-14T10:23:27-07:00","id":1463849,"title":"Being Frozen in Time... with Accents","content":"A thought struck me after my usual Wednesday game... don't accents have an element of muscle memory?<br /> <br /> If this is the case, would it mean that a vampire would be forever stuck with their accent from their breathing days, or whatever vocal range when they were Embraced? I guess if you Embraced a voice actor they would have a large range, but to do anything other than their usual voice would require the effort of a performance.<br /> <br /> If so, this would have an impact on the ability to express languages. I have visions of a vampire from the southern US speaking several languages fluently, but never able to shake that drawl...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T10:54:34-07:00","id":1463855,"title":"","content":"Like many things in the game, it's less about strict realism and more about the needs of the genre. Is it better to have the elder vampire giving some kind of tells that reveals he's an incredibly ancient Anglo-Saxon warrior, Roman Senator, or an Elizabethan era playwright? Or to allow the elder vampire to be able to blend into society as if they were a member of that time and culture? Both kinds of vampires work fine in the game.<br /> <br /> There are people who will always speak a foreign language with an accent even though they are fluent, and there are people who will speak it like a native despite learning it late in life. There are plenty of people who will keep their regional accent after moving to another place, and people who can easily switch between accents when needed. So vampires should be able to do the same. It's really based on how someone wants to portray a specific character, regardless if it is a PC or NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T23:26:11-07:00","id":1463966,"title":"","content":"As an ESL teacher, no. It's entirely possible for you to pick up a new language at any point in life and get to the point where you sound exactly like a native speaker. <br /> While myths say otherwise, studies show adults are better at learning <b>second</b> languages than children, and it's entirely possible to train yourself to understand new <b>phonemes</b> (sounds that can distinguish one word for another; with foreign languages you might not pick up on different sounds that seem obvious to natives, and they in return might not pick up on different sounds that seem obvious to you. One big example being japanese struggling with l and R sounds in english, because they don't use those sounds in Japanese) (If for some reason someone doesn't have a first language by the time they're an adult, that's a massive issue they can't work around, but first language acquisition shouldn't be confused with second language acquisition) <br /> <br /> The reason why children are thought to be better than adults at learning other languages (other than confusing the issues with late first language acquisition and second language acquisition) is 1: Children have more time to learn and 2: Children are less self conscious/embarrassed when it comes to trying to pick up new sounds. <br /> <br /> In the context of vampires <br /> 1: they're often smarter and more perceptive than their mortal adult selves, just as adults are smarter and more developed than their child selves. <br /> 2: They're under huge pressure to fit in so it's more embarrassing to not have the accent than to try and learn the accent. <br /> 3: Vampires can still accumulate skills so I don't see why they wouldn't be able to gain new muscle memories. <br /> <br /> While we're here, it's also better to learn explicitly than implicitly. IE being taught the rules for grammar is better than just being around people talking and hoping you'll pick the rules up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T08:15:09-07:00","id":1464033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463849-being-frozen-in-time-with-accents?p=1463966#post1463966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it's entirely possible to train yourself to understand new <b>phonemes</b> (sounds that can distinguish one word for another; with foreign languages you might not pick up on different sounds that seem obvious to natives, and they in return might not pick up on different sounds that seem obvious to you. One big example being japanese struggling with l and R sounds in english, because they don't use those sounds in Japanese)</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this well, as English in fact is my second language. There are a bunch of very subtle phonemes that don't exist in Portuguese, not to say a huge difference on the standard pronunciation of every single vowel, but the greatest challenge is the TH. On the other side, English speakers struggle a lot with Portuguese phonemes, especially \u00c3O.<br /> <br /> I distinctly remember at least two old corebooks referencing at some point that a vampire is actually quite able to change accent as to be a better predator, although it was lost in some fluffy text instead of a rule. But otherwise any difficulty to adapt is represented in game terms as a Flaw, so it shouldn't be taken as default for most vampires anyway. Vampires learn new skills as normal, and real people change and adapt accent fairly easily, not only when learning new languages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}